        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सिरा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सिरा — sirā — \"a vein\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रक्तं सिरासु वहति। raktaṃ sirāsu vahati. Blood flows in the veins."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सिरा (sirā) comes from the root √sṛ, \"to flow\": MW's first sense is \"a stream\", then \"any tubular vessel of the body, a vein, an artery\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
